  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Changing Workforce: Split the Job into Stages",
    "description": "Handle workers joining, leaving, or changing hours after part of a job is already complete.",
    "teachingApproach": "Use a two-stage timeline. First calculate how much work the original crew has already completed; only the remainder moves into stage two. Cover absence delays, extra-worker recovery, known fraction complete, early completion due higher daily output, and simultaneous changes in workforce and hours. Make the learner check the final combined work against one full job.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 32,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 15, Chain Rule. Approved scope: Teach stage-based chain rule for jobs whose workforce changes. Cover absentees causing delay, extra workers needed after a known fraction of work is completed, workers added to recover a deadline, a team finishing early because daily output rises, and two-stage problems where hours per day also change. Emphasize that the first stage has already consumed part of the work, so only the remaining work belongs in the second chain. Include forward checks against the promised deadline."
  },
  "scriptId": "cr-06-changing-workforce-deadlines",
